  "content": "<div id=\"readability-page-1\" class=\"page\"><div><article id=\"article\"><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://d39wtn5cxihhz5.cloudfront.net/content/800Pasted-image-20260817122017.jpeg\" srcset=\"https://d39wtn5cxihhz5.cloudfront.net/content/800Pasted-image-20260817122017.jpeg 800w, https://d39wtn5cxihhz5.cloudfront.net/content/667Pasted-image-20260817122017.jpeg 667w, https://d39wtn5cxihhz5.cloudfront.net/content/534Pasted-image-20260817122017.jpeg 534w, https://d39wtn5cxihhz5.cloudfront.net/content/401Pasted-image-20260817122017.jpeg 401w, https://d39wtn5cxihhz5.cloudfront.net/content/268Pasted-image-20260817122017.jpeg 268w, https://d39wtn5cxihhz5.cloudfront.net/content/135Pasted-image-20260817122017.jpeg 135w\"></p><p><small>Published: 2026-08-17</small></p><blockquote><p> In contrast to this maniac on the front page of Hacker News: <a href=\"https://ben.balter.com/2026/08/17/how-i-over-engineered-my-book/\">How I Over-Engineered My Book</a><br></p></blockquote><p>I typed the first draft of each chapter into Obsidian. Then I copy/pasted it into Word. When it was done, I dragged and dropped it into Box, which is where Manning stores its author's manuscripts. </p><p>Then I kept doing that until it was done. </p><p>It looked something like this: </p><p>It's done! <a href=\"https://www.manning.com/books/data-oriented-programming-in-java\">Buy it here!</a> Give me your money! </p></article></div></div>",
